+# Bounded automatic approval (v0.2.21, development_not_for_deployment)
+
+Goal: a REQUEST that GPT publishes to the PRIVATE repository gets its `APPROVAL_SIG.json` and `READY.md` from the existing Windows signer without a
+Telegram button or a manual Claude Code step, and the SAME single GitHub LIVE watcher then runs exactly one independent review.
+
+**Default: the feature does not exist.** Without an `auto_approval` section in the watcher config nothing changes. With the section but the protected
+delegation file saying `enabled: false` (the default), nothing is signed. **Nothing written to GitHub can enable, widen or extend it.**
+
+## What it may do, and what it may never do
+- May: for a REQUEST that has no READY yet, inside a local delegation, publish `APPROVAL_SIG.json` (create-only, read back) and then `READY.md`
+  (create-only, LAST, read back). The existing `SOURCE_PIN.json` that GPT published is used as it is and never overwritten.
+- Never: start a review (the unchanged READY checks, the N1 remote dispatch reservation and the single model call stay as they are), change a key,
+  the trust root, a ceiling or a policy, or retry blindly after a doubt.
+
+## Order of every decision (all read-only until the reservation)
+1. Delegation file readable, ACL protected (no Everyone/Users/Authenticated Users write on the file or its folder; read through the Win32 DACL, SID
+   based), schema `AUTO_DELEGATION_V1`, `enabled: true`, not expired.
+2. The REQUEST was FIRST SEEN while the delegation was enabled, and its pinned commit A is not older than `enabled_at` (no retroactive start; a
+   request seen while the feature was off stays excluded forever).
+3. Repository: the numeric id the server reports now = `SOURCE_PIN.repo_id` = `delegation.repo_id`; `SOURCE_PIN` schema/commit well formed.
+4. Package: size and sha256 equal the REQUEST, ZIP CRC, the engine's credential scan, `safe_extract`, size limit 5 MiB.
+5. Commit A: the REQUEST and the package bytes at the pinned commit equal the bytes on `main` today.
+6. No earlier history: no APPROVAL_SIG/READY/dispatch/receipt/result on the remote, no local job, no earlier reservation.
+7. The pure gate `auto_policy.assess` (GPT prototype, byte-identical): scope allow-lists, `POLICY-STATIC-V1` only, 1 call, attempt 1, per request <= $1,
+   day <= 2 calls / $3, month <= $10 (limits can only be equal to or stricter than the product ceilings), counting the watcher's own recorded dispatches.
+8. The official validator on the READY text that WILL be published (bytes fixed before signing).
+9. Atomic reservation (`BEGIN IMMEDIATE`, one row per request and revision, day/month ceilings inside the same transaction).
+10. Re-check (delegation still enabled and unexpired, repository id unchanged) -> sign with the existing `tools.approval_signer` -> verify with the
+    watcher's own `verify_approval` -> store the approval and READY bytes -> re-check -> publish approval -> re-check -> publish READY last.
+
+## Stops
+Any failure after the reservation ends in `UNCERTAIN` (event `AUTO_SIGNING_UNCERTAIN`, listed in the notification events): no automatic retry, no
+re-signature. The only automatic resumes: a reservation without a stored signature may sign ONE more time (nothing was ever published); a stored,
+unexpired approval or READY is published with the same bytes. An expired stored approval is never re-signed.
+
+## Configuration (example, nothing secret)
+```json
+"auto_approval": {
+  "delegation_file": "C:/ProgramData/cowork/auto_delegation.json",
+  "valid_hours": 2,
+  "signer": {"private_key_file": "...approver.key.enc", "key_id": "cowork-approver-1", "repo_id": "1451933830",
+             "passphrase_dpapi_file": "...approver.pass.dpapi", "dpapi_entropy": "cowork-approver-v1"}
+}
+```
+`delegation_file` (protected, written by the user, never by GitHub or this program):
+```json
+{"schema": "AUTO_DELEGATION_V1", "enabled": false, "repo_id": "1451933830", "branch": "main",
+ "projects": ["<explicit work ids>"], "skills": ["<explicit skill ids>"], "policy": "POLICY-STATIC-V1",
+ "enabled_at": "2026-11-16T00:00:00+09:00", "expires_at": "2026-12-16T00:00:00+09:00",
+ "max_request_usd": 1.0, "max_day_calls": 2, "max_day_usd": 3.0, "max_month_usd": 10.0}
+```
+`config-check` prints the state without any path of a secret. `acl_check: "skip"` exists for isolated tests only and is printed as a warning.
+
+## Enabling procedure (after an explicit user approval; not part of this candidate)
+install with `enabled: false` -> let one watch cycle pass (every pending REQUEST is recorded as "seen while off") -> set `enabled: true` and
+`enabled_at` to now. Revoke by setting `enabled: false` (takes effect at the next check, also between signing and publishing).
+
+## Rollback
+Remove the `auto_approval` section (or keep `enabled: false`) and restart; the two new tables stay unused. Restore the previous package folder from
+its ZIP (byte copy). Nothing else of the operating watcher, database, Task, Notifier or key is changed by this feature.
+
+## Known limits (see the result document)
+The signing capability runs inside the watcher process of the same Windows account that reads GitHub-controlled input; the protection is the
+delegation gate plus the fail-closed order above, not a separate trust domain. The installed Notifier has its own event list: add
+`AUTO_SIGNING_UNCERTAIN` there when the feature is enabled.
